title AMUS6 — Constel switchboard: a whole local constellation, routed by name
prompt Keaton set the recursion loop on the 1024-round itinerary and six-season double-seat: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, make progress before checking in, send often as its own signed round, stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think AMUS5 (channel) landed and sent — two piers agree over a bounded byte stream, one frame at a time. Its road-on named the socket as the next rung, yet the socket crosses the Comlink seam (seed/comlink/, a real transport) and is a custody gate — not agent-doable. Lindy-first crux-first among the agent-doable: Constel is named for a CONSTELLATION (many piers), and every rung so far joined exactly two. Standing up three or more fake piers meeting through one shared medium is the module's namesake promise, purely local, and a strict predecessor to any socket — prove the many-pier logic pure on the bench before metal, exactly as the tree proves every value before hardware.
think The one genuinely new concern a network of many piers forces and nothing before it did: route a frame to the right pier BY NAME. A Switchboard is a bounded set of per-pier channel.Channel mailboxes over an AMUS1 roster — deliver(to, frame) pushes onto a pier's inbound mailbox, receive(from) reads exactly one whole frame off a pier's own mailbox (delegating the stream discipline to channel.read_frame), a name no roster holds refuses NoSuchPier before a byte moves. handshake_through drives the whole AMUS4 handshake with the switchboard as the two piers' ONLY shared medium — each frame delivered to the other's mailbox, received off the recipient's own.
think Re-designated the socket: AMUS6 was prose-only (unbuilt) for the socket; the switchboard is the next BUILT rung, so it seats as AMUS6 and the socket becomes plainly "the socket, gated, later." Dated fossils (the AMUS5 design doc and channel.rye comment saying "AMUS6, the real Comlink socket") keep their words under accrete-never-break; only the living README moves forward. This is how the tree already grows past its plan (BUHR's eleven journeys).
obs The switchboard only ROUTES; it never re-checks a frame, so the two AMUS3 trust gates (Sha256 integrity + the naming-law border at wire.deframe_*) stay the only trust boundary. The bystander test is the load-bearing new proof: after two of three piers complete a handshake, the third's mailbox holds zero bytes — a delivered frame reached exactly one mailbox, not all. And a pier reads only its own mail: a frame for p1 waits in p1's box (== gf.len) and is absent from p0's and p2's.
obs Witness GREEN on the FIRST run — no red this lap (AMUS4 and AMUS5 each caught one on metal; this rung reused their proven values/bounds, so nothing new to trip on). Five blocks proven: a constellation of three stands up (lawful whole, no vowel, three empty mailboxes); two members agree routed through the switchboard and both principals' mailboxes drain; a stranger's name refuses NoSuchPier at deliver and receive; a pier reads only its own mail; and a greeting routed through a mailbox but carrying a smuggled vowel (digest fixed up) still refuses VowelPresent at the border. Witness GREEN, TAME bans clean (new file not in the zero-assert ratchet list), width exit 0.
obs Kept docs synced (docs-implementation-sync): constel/README.md gains the switchboard rung, the run block lists amus_switchboard_witness, Status and Kin weave include AMUS6, and the road-on now names ONLY the socket as the remaining rung — marked plainly as the one that stops for Keaton's word because it crosses the Comlink seam.
loom witness=amus_switchboard_witness blocks=5 mailboxes=8 max_channel_bytes=252 greeting_frame_bytes=64 constellation_piers=3 wall_ms_note=selftest under a second after build
file active-designing/20260814-045802_amus6-constel-switchboard-multi-pier.md the AMUS6 design — the switchboard, the route-by-name move, the six proofs
file constel/switchboard.rye AMUS6 — a bounded per-pier mailbox set that routes a handshake among many fake piers, composing roster.rye + channel.rye + exchange.rye
file tools/amus_switchboard_witness.rish the GREEN witness for AMUS6
file constel/README.md kept synced — the switchboard rung, run block, Status, Kin, and a socket-only road-on marked as Keaton's check-in
recommend keep-going — AMUS6 (switchboard) is GREEN and sends as its own signed round; the whole pure-local Constel stack now stands up a real many-pier constellation (name · roster · handshake · wire · exchange · channel · switchboard). The next AMUS rung, the socket, genuinely crosses the Comlink seam and stays Keaton's hand; plenty of agent-doable double-seat work remains (a Constel gossip/consensus rung over the switchboard, or a fresh Season A/D/F journey), so the loop continues rather than stopping. Clock note: America/New_York read 20260814.045802, earlier than the prior newest 080900; the one-clock monotonic law honored by stamping 081400, just after the work it follows.
